.temp/resources/TASK-260715-uopycx/TASK-260715-uopycx_pinned-baseline-audit.md:375:## 9. Callback ingress/egress fork feasibility
.temp/resources/TASK-260715-uopycx/TASK-260715-uopycx_pinned-baseline-audit.md:377:A minimal callback fork is technically feasible because packet I/O is localized:
.temp/resources/TASK-260715-uopycx/TASK-260715-uopycx_pinned-baseline-audit.md:379:- ingress: `lwip_io_task_entry` → `hev_tunnel_read` → `netif.input`;
.temp/resources/TASK-260715-uopycx/TASK-260715-uopycx_pinned-baseline-audit.md:380:- egress: lwIP netif callback → `netif_output_handler` → `hev_tunnel_write`.
.temp/resources/TASK-260715-uopycx/TASK-260715-uopycx_pinned-baseline-audit.md:383:at that boundary while preserving HEV's scheduler thread, pbuf ownership, return
.temp/resources/TASK-260715-uopycx/TASK-260715-uopycx_pinned-baseline-audit.md:384:codes, shutdown wakeup, and IPv4/IPv6 classification. Calling arbitrary Swift
.temp/resources/TASK-260715-uopycx/TASK-260715-uopycx_pinned-baseline-audit.md:388:Feasibility is not justification. A fork proposal must attach all of:
.temp/resources/TASK-260715-uopycx/TASK-260715-uopycx_pinned-baseline-audit.md:390:1. Instruments evidence that socketpair copies or syscalls are a material share
.temp/resources/TASK-260715-uopycx/TASK-260715-uopycx_pinned-baseline-audit.md:391:   of CPU/energy/latency or cause the memory gate to fail.
.temp/resources/TASK-260715-uopycx/TASK-260715-uopycx_pinned-baseline-audit.md:392:2. An apples-to-apples physical iPhone and macOS benchmark of unmodified fd path
.temp/resources/TASK-260715-uopycx/TASK-260715-uopycx_pinned-baseline-audit.md:393:   versus callback prototype, including IPv4/IPv6, TCP/UDP, MTU matrix,
