+# TASK-260715-2jatnd handoff evidence
+
+## Outcome
+
+Ready for independent review. The task-scoped ADR records the macOS-first M0
+Bridge gate as passed under ADR-024, while preserving MTU 8500 as a failed
+default candidate and physical iPhone, NAT64, sleep/wake, and whole-extension
+memory as blocked/deferred rows. It selects MTU 1500, requested/effective
+32768-byte socket buffers, 64-packet/5-ms pump budgets, HEV values
+24576/4096/2, and an initial measured 500-session ceiling. Unmodified pinned HEV
+is retained; fork authorization is rejected because no qualifying Instruments
+or callback-prototype evidence exists.
+
+## Repository artifacts
+
+- `docs/TASK-260715-2jatnd_m0-bridge-hev-decision-adr.md` — task-scoped decision,
+  gate/evidence matrix, configuration, pins/notices, no-fork disposition,
+  residual risks, revalidation triggers, decomposition traceability, and exact
+  downstream tasks.
+- `.spec/decisions.md` — ADR-015 accepted with MTU 1500 and the task-scoped ADR
+  as authority.
+- `.spec/packet-plane.md` — evidence-backed initial YAML, socket-buffer, and work
+  budgets; injectable later tuning retained.
+- `README.md` — decision discovery link.
+- `LOGBOOK.md` — decision, memory boundary, no-fork disposition, and deferred
+  gaps recorded.
+
+ADR SHA-256:
+`aaceefe38a715025de331a287f47cd5f5e142ad0e45906df4058705ebd10e78c`.
+
+## Evidence synthesis
+
+- Accepted physical MTU source: `TASK-260715-gyg51r_rev4-results.md` plus
+  `TASK-260715-gyg51r_review-rev4-verdict.md` and independent raw matrix.
+- Accepted physical memory source: `TASK-260715-135rr8_rev4-results.md` plus
+  `TASK-260715-135rr8_review-verdict-rev4.md` and three independent matrices.
+- Structural/test sources: accepted resources from `TASK-260715-uopycx`,
+  `TASK-260715-p89bdj`, `TASK-260715-3o0co4`, `TASK-260715-1vv52g`,
+  `TASK-260715-3dn813`, `TASK-260715-35wctc`, `TASK-260715-52h8i3`,
+  `TASK-260720-9xy8yx`, `BUG-260720-2p4fln`, and
+  `BUG-260720-24f9w6`.
+- Historical failed runs remain attached to the source tasks. The ADR names
+  red/deferred rows independently and does not average them into the macOS pass.
+
+## Completeness and decomposition review
+
+Every Story task has one atomic deliverable and a concrete trace to
+`.spec/packet-plane.md`, `.spec/validation.md`, `.spec/security-privacy.md`, or
+`.spec/delivery.md`. The only beyond-literal-spec Bugs each carry a written gap
+and out-of-scope record in the ADR. The sole research task names the exact open
+pin/configuration/build/license question. Dependencies already connect the
+implementation/test chain to both accepted physical gates and this decision;
+no task, dependency, research item, or diagram was added. This is the smallest
+decomposition that preserves provenance and maps every requirement.
+
+Direct dependency edges released by this decision are
+`TASK-260720-1qhxqa`, `TASK-260715-12x6oq`, `TASK-260715-2xx2tk`,
+`TASK-260715-38o3xg`, and `TASK-260715-1pn983`. Each retains its other blockers;
+M1 production composition is not claimed ready until the binding task accepts
+all required M0 inputs.
+
+## Validation performed in this run
+
+- Tool readiness: `task-board --help`, exit 0; log
+  `.temp/TASK-260715-2jatnd/task-board-readiness.log`.
+- Story-base freshness: `git fetch origin main`, exit 0; Story HEAD, local
+  `main`, fetched `origin/main`, and merge base all equal
+  `489c924a16e775d8012db806717815e4e7eb92ad`; log SHA-256
